","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/commits/6727af91066b1241df696358187e4f06c3e8ef9b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:03:23Z","email":"3084745+colinhacks@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Colin McDonnell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:03:23Z","email":"3084745+colinhacks@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Colin McDonnell"},"message":"fix: seal .cts output, and stop settling live bindings\n\nTwo gaps in where sealing reached, both reproduced before fixing.\n\nTypeScript names pre-rename output by source extension, so a `.cts` module\narrives at `writeFile` already called `.cjs` and never entered the `.js` branch.\nIt is also emitted by *both* passes, and the ESM pass writes last — so sealing\nnow keys off the output extension rather than the pass, and the ESM pass carries\nthe flag too. A `.mjs` output is real ESM and stays excluded.\n\nTypeScript compiles a named re-export to an unconditional getter onto the source\nbinding, and the settle loop cannot tell one that forwards to a live `export let`\nfrom one that forwards to a constant. Snapshotting a live one made\n`require(pkg).counter` report `0` forever while `import` reported `2`. A build\ncontaining any mutable exported binding now gives up settling everywhere and\ntakes only the freeze, which keeps both module systems agreeing.\n\nThe mutable fixture moves to its own directory, since one live binding changes\nthe whole build''s behavior and would have masked the zero-accessor assertion.","tree":{"sha":"fbf19add809ef71d531c8405d9dc765f14d6746b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/git/trees/fbf19add809ef71d531c8405d9dc765f14d6746b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/git/commits/6727af91066b1241df696358187e4f06c3e8ef9b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"c