.com/users/colinhacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/commits/e877302fe2a2ca5ec16a895168f9b5b6ebc9b155/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T17:37:59Z","email":"3084745+colinhacks@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Colin McDonnell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T17:37:59Z","email":"3084745+colinhacks@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Colin McDonnell"},"message":"feat: add sealCjsExports, settling the CommonJS re-export accessors into data properties\n\nTypeScript emits every re-export as a `__createBinding` accessor, so a consumer\nthat calls an API off the namespace reads the function through a getter on every\ncall. The engine never sees a constant callee and the call is not inlined. On\nzod that is 35.9M ops/s under `require` against 115.5M under `import`, with 252\nof the 255 exports on its `index.cjs` being accessors.\n\n`__createBinding` copies a source descriptor instead of wrapping it whenever\nthat descriptor is a non-writable, non-configurable data property, so a module\nthat seals its own exports on the way out settles the whole re-export chain\nabove it. `Object.freeze` handles the data properties in one step; the loop\nbeside it handles the configurable accessors that `export { a } from \"...\"`\nleaves behind.\n\nReassigning `module.exports` to a flat object settles the same exports in one\nplace, but it blinds `cjs-module-lexer`: named imports from ESM stop resolving\nand attw reports a missing `export =`. The fixture pins that by importing named\nbindings out of the built .cjs from an ESM subprocess.\n\nOff by default. Sealing is observable — every export becomes non-writable and\nnon-configurable, the namespace is frozen, and loading costs a few milliseconds\nmore.","tree":{"sha":"942ab4efe515072295a74ab57e9fabd072ff806d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/git/trees/942ab4efe515072295a74ab57e9fabd072ff806d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/git/commits/e877302fe2a2ca5ec16a895168f9b5b6ebc9b155","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks","id":3084745,"login":"colinhacks","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwODQ3NDU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/colinhacks","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks/zshy/commit/e877302fe2a2ca5ec16a895168f9b5b6ebc9b155","node_id":"C_kwDOPCIyLdoAKGU4NzczMDJmZTJhMmNhNWVjMTZhODk1MTY4ZjliNWI2ZWJjOWIxNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/colinhacks/zshy/commit/acce27d85eda066ff75b52282019086c6ae10844","sha":"acce27d85eda066ff75b52282019086c6ae10844","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/commits/acce27d85eda066ff75b52282019086c6ae10844"}],"sha":"e877302fe2a2ca5ec16a895168f9b5b6ebc9b155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/colinhacks/zshy/commits/e877302fe2a2ca5ec16a895168f9b5b6ebc9b155"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3084745?v=4","events_url":"https://api.git