ommit":{"author":{"date":"2025-07-11T12:17:36Z","email":"108800804+ermolaev-frontend@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Evgeniy Ermolaev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-07-11T12:17:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"This PR introduces a comprehensive color picker functionality to Draftly, allowing users to select from a predefined color palette when drawing shapes. The implementation includes a new ColorPicker component, enhanced color management throughout the application, and various code improvements for better maintainability and performance.\n\n* Refactor Draftly and Pencil classes to improve shape handling and drawing logic. Update clearCanvas method to deselect shapes instead of requesting a draw, and simplify drawNewShape method by directly pushing points to the array.\n\n* Enhance DraftlyWrapper and Draftly classes to support dynamic color selection. Introduce selectedColor state in EditorPage and pass it to DraftlyWrapper. Update drawing logic in Draftly to use currentColor for shapes. Add ColorPicker component in Toolbar for color selection.\n\n* Refactor Toolbar styles and ColorPicker component. Update ColorPickerProps to include onColorChange prop and enhance Toolbar layout with improved styling for better mobile responsiveness.\n\n* Refactor DraftlyWrapper to remove selectedColor prop and manage color state within EditorPage. Update color setting logic to ensure dynamic color updates in Draftly instance.\n\n* Refactor EditorPage to use useCallback for handleColorChange function, optimizing performance. Update ColorPicker component to use memo for improved rendering efficiency.\n\n* Enhance Draftly, Pencil, and Rectangle classes for improved shape handling and user experience. Add edge detection logic in Rectangle for better interaction, update drawNewShape in Pencil to include points in patch, and refine Draftly''s pointer handling with a requestDraw call after pointer up.\n\n* Refactor color handling in Draftly and Rectangle classes to utilize BASE_PALETTE for default colors. Update EditorPage to manage tool and color states more effectively, removing the ColorPicker component. Enhance Toolbar layout for better mobile responsiveness.\n\n* Refactor EditorPage import structure and remove unused EditorPage component files. Simplify the import path for EditorPage in App.tsx.\n\n* Refactor tool handling in EditorPage to utilize handleTool function for improved clarity and maintainability. Update dependencies in useEffect for better performance.\n\n* Refactor canvasUtils to remove unused Catmull-Rom and Douglas-Peucker functions, streamline shape initialization with BASE_PALETTE for colors, and enhance color handling in getInitialShapes function. Update Rectangle class to simplify bounds checking logic.\n\n* Remove redundant patch call in drawNewShape method of Pencil class to streamline shape drawing logic.\n\n* Remove tests for Catmull-Rom and Douglas-Peucker functions in canvasUtils.test.ts, retaining only the hashStringToSeed tests for improved test suite clarity and focus.\n\n* Refactor Draftly class to use static properties for INITIAL_SHAPES_COUNT and DRAWING_TOOLS, enhancing code clarity and consistency in shape initialization.","tree":{"sha":"5fb942014348e4977d6e539a3be13f306250dddb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ermolaev-frontend/draftly/git/trees/5fb942014348e4977d6e539a3be13f306250dddb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ermolaev-frontend/draftly/git/commits/2f02da40bc564195f1798440862f74c2c636f056","verification":{"payload":"tree 5fb942014348e4977d6e539a3be13f306250dddb\nparent 12ef2f6601d7a99215a5978411f27ad7d95d46ae\nauthor Evgeniy Ermolaev <108800804+ermolaev-frontend@users.noreply.github.com> 1752236256 +0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1752236256 +0400\n\nThis PR introduces a comprehensive color picker functionality to Draftly, allowing users to select from a predefined color palette when drawing shapes. The implementation includes a new ColorPicker component, enhanced color management throughout the application, and various code improvements for better maintainability and performance.\n\n* Refactor Draftly and Pencil classes to improve shape handling and drawing logic. Update clearCanvas method to deselect shapes instead of requesting a draw, and simplify drawNewShape method by directly pushing points to the array.\n\n* Enhance DraftlyWrapper and Draftly classes to support dynamic color selection. Introduce selectedColor state in EditorPage and pass it to DraftlyWrapper. Update drawing logic in Draftly to use currentColor for shapes. Add ColorPicker component in Toolbar for color selection.\n\n* Refactor Toolbar styles and ColorPicker component. Update ColorPickerProps to include onColorChange prop and enhance Toolbar layout with improved styling for better mobile responsiveness.\n\n* Refactor DraftlyWrapper to remove selectedColor prop and manage color state within EditorPage. Update color setting logic to ensure dynamic color updates in Draftly instance.\n\n* Refactor EditorPage to use useCallback for handleColorChange function, optimizing performance. Update ColorPicker component to use memo for improved rendering efficiency.\n\n* Enhance Draftly, Pencil, and Rectangle classes for improved shape handling and user experience. Add edge detection logic in Rectangle for better interaction, update drawNewShape in Pencil to include points in patch, and refine Draftly''s pointer handling with a requestDraw call after pointer up.\n\n* Refactor color handling in Draftly and Rectangle classes to utilize BASE_PALETTE for default colors. Update EditorPage to manage tool and color states more effectively, removing the ColorPicker component. Enhance Toolbar layout for better mobile responsiveness.\n\n* Refactor EditorPage import structure and remove unused EditorPage component files. Simplify the import path for EditorPage in App.tsx.\n\n* Refactor tool handling in EditorPage to utilize handleTool function for improved clarity and maintainability. Update dependencies in useEffect for better performance.\n\n* Refactor canvasUtils to remove unused Catmull-Rom and Douglas-Peucker functions, streamline shape initialization with BASE_PALETTE for colors, and enhance color handling in getInitialShapes function. Update Rectangle class to simplify bounds checking logic.\n\n* Remove redundant patch call in drawNewShape method of Pencil class to streamline shape drawing logic.\n\n* Remove tests for Catmull-Rom and Douglas-Peucker functions in canvasUtils.test.ts, retaining only the hashStringToSeed tests for improved test suite clarity and focus.\n\n* Refactor Draftly class to use static properties for INITIAL_SHAPES_COUNT and DRAWING_TOOLS, enhancing code clarity and consistency in shape initialization.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJocQDgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA89UQAAZSnudjI0tuMtBIlDURsrf5\nKVfanuPwxAHabEonTN7ql4Zx71H4Y228rLTiJ5D8Vl3SFS7C190WESaz3vBglqFE\nGFBilnx9tMCZ5ypgX8eNC9J9Nn7OHeboK6YTsIkG9Hh11ycPlbVFdIyrxo7NUtzE\ndj3atfIOvxrjgDujE1S7VqFxv4/SsKBR/xjwyarA8w7i721O3faOuWwHezUSs8Pt\n6/xTBLjXFGqRMtrDebUDbmbYqcbZje3oJ9BgUIzxsU2LMRFjntMiADa9ptXRXI2l\nkO7dncSh8MD05AeDpswhwsGA8Ir3okcx611lA5WPJNcJJdR+5W1vh+vcAzuowIPG\nvGF6+Zgn2No2pgBDxxyRtESPdIwrfg2EHtOQEkf9ZgQGzmW/WU2REgHV6BTV0jkZ\nKAEz579BamRxcD3AE5RSOrQN+k6ELiuP0ph9VVvrheYaHKSUBAw1ZwCIjWu46H25\nxKEomhTkmf4RJz36GkQtHQ7nfP6yeaFcviI8ds6vBF0gtPSY3+duwl5M1LTK6Ybs\nSM4KnyB2YOpNp11DQdi843q8h5f3i67/0xNBrex2pw80FL4WtW4H791nbaNgsF9G\nNvIGB34H/f8pZD4jOckBSKh6uw5zouKlf5VRJiIaD1LRmL7/ycxkBi2h7fqEZ+JT\nGCL2971y/VLk6W56hN+C\n=alkV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2025-07-11T12:17:37Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","g